{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"agent_message","text":"The key probes identify the two-colour moving object as the avatar; each move shifts it four pixels. The right passage and lower passage both block it. I also tested the displayed pattern: clicking its three cells clears the input, but neither passage opens from the entry position. I’ll test whether the pattern’s effect depends on where the avatar stands.\n\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat > probe_context.py <<'PY'\nfrom probe_level3 import harness,entry\nfrom perception import arr,safe_step,frame_delta\nfrom legs import enter_displayed_pattern\n\ndef probe(e):\n entry(e)\n for name,path in [('entry',[]),('right',[4,4]),('bottom',[3,3,2,2]),('top',[1,1,1])]:\n  c=e.clone()\n  for a in path:safe_step(c,a)\n  base=arr(c.frame()).copy()\n  enter_displayed_pattern(c,6)\n  print(name,'pattern',frame_delta(base,c.frame()))\n  for key in [1,2,3,4]:\n   d=c.clone();b=arr(d.frame()).copy();safe_step(d,key);print('key',key,frame_delta(b,d.frame()))\nprint(harness.A.run_program('sc25',probe)[::2])\nPY\npython probe_context.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
